  "answer": "### Short Answer\nA corporation must satisfy specific conditions to claim a bad debt as a deductible expense, primarily that the debt must be considered worthless and must have been previously included in gross income.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practice, this means that corporations should maintain thorough records of debts owed to them, including any collection attempts made. When a debt is deemed uncollectible, the corporation can then deduct this amount from its gross income, thereby reducing its taxable income for the year. This deduction can provide significant tax relief, especially for businesses that extend credit as part of their operations.",
